        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Initially, if the option \"research schedule directly\" is selected, then the action to be taken is \"Research schedule\". If the option is not selected, then \"provide indications\" and proceed with the research schedule."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures process start, initial conditional split on option selection, both resulting action paths, and flow convergence. Structural nodes and guards correctly abstract the stated logic."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "guard:b2->n8",
        "guard:b2->n9",
        "action:n8",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After validating the schedule, check if the schedule is satisfactory. If it is not, then perform the action \"Research schedule\". If it is, then proceed with writing a ticket order to SNCF."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the schedule validation step and the subsequent binary decision on satisfactoriness, with correct negative (research) and positive (write order) arms."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n11",
        "guard:b3->n12",
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the schedule is not satisfactory, perform the action \"Research schedule\". If it is still not satisfactory, then \"provide indications\". Alternatively, if the schedule is satisfactory, write a ticket order to SNCF."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the explicit alternative/restatement provided later in the text. Preserves the same branching logic and outcomes without changing overall behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13",
        "guard:b4->e1",
        "guard:b4->n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After writing the ticket order, validate it. Check if the ticket order is approved. If it is not, then the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the initial ticket validation and first approval gate, correctly terminating the flow on rejection."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n16",
        "guard:b5->e2",
        "guard:b5->n19"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it is approved, then validate the ticket order. Check again if the ticket order is approved. If it is not, then the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the iterative validation step and second approval gate, matching the source's repeated check pattern."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n19",
        "guard:b6->e3",
        "guard:b6->e4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it is approved, then validate the ticket order. Check once more if the ticket order is approved. If it is, then the process ends. If it is not, then the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the third validation, final approval check, and dual termination paths. e5 is unconnected structural noise and does not affect behaviour, so it is safely grouped as a match per relaxation guidelines."
    }
